{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the sons of Aaron, Nadav and Avihu, took, etc.</b> It intends to inform us of the source of their error, which is for two reasons: the first — that they were priests, upon whom the service devolves, and this is why it begins by saying ״the sons of Aaron.״ The second — that they were great in deed and equivalent to Moshe and Aaron, as they of blessed memory said (Torat Kohanim here, Acharei Mot 63), and as they said in the holy Zohar (Acharei Mot 56) that they were on a lofty level by virtue of their deeds, and this is what it says ״Nadav and Avihu.״ This quality is not found in Elazar and Itamar, for although they are sons of Aaron, they do not have a level of their own like Nadav and Avihu. And so you will find that they of blessed memory expounded (Torat Kohanim, Leviticus 10:16) on what is written ״And Moshe was angry with Elazar, etc. the remaining,״ etc. — see their words there. And with this strength they entered, and they were precise to enter both of them together to magnify their merit, and they did not wish to take fire from the altar. They said: perhaps it is not fitting to take from it except for the obligatory incense-offering; therefore they brought it from outside." "<b>And they placed upon it.</b> And it does not say ״upon them,״ as it says ״and they put in them,״ etc. — ״and they placed upon them״ — it refers back to the fire that it mentioned nearby, since the strictness is about strange fire; therefore it attributed the act to it." "<b>Strange, which He did not command.</b> Meaning, and what is its strangeness? That HaShem did not command it. Or perhaps that if they had taken fire from upon the altar, HaShem would not have been so insistent about the matter — or perhaps He would have been insistent for another reason. Further, it may intend along this line: ״strange fire, which He did not command them״ to do so — and this itself is its strangeness."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:54:48.669736945Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}